WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.139 --> 00:00:07.139
In this section, we're going to discuss media profiles and implementing them for use in your ICVFX stage.

2
00:00:07.139 --> 00:00:13.140
On the LANTE stage, one of the things that we actually connect through is the Aja Kona 5 interface.

3
00:00:13.140 --> 00:00:26.140
So we use the KeyPro Ultra 12G, and this piece of hardware connects all of our devices, our camera, and our master clock into the computer so that everything is synchronized through our Kona 5 card.

4
00:00:26.140 --> 00:00:38.140
Our input, output, genlock, and pass-through SDI information needs to be noted that when in use, the media profile that we're about to build will separate the signals onto separate internal SDI channels.

5
00:00:38.140 --> 00:00:46.140
So when we set this up, we're going to set our input to SDI 1, output to SDI 2, and our genlock to SDI 4.

6
00:00:46.140 --> 00:00:49.140
Now let's move into the engine to set up our media profile.

7
00:00:49.140 --> 00:00:57.140
So to start with a media profile, I want to take a look at the project that we're working with, and this is our stage 11801-503b.

8
00:00:57.140 --> 00:01:08.140
It's a clean project that we've been working from, and we will actually begin building from having assembled our end display configuration and adding in a media profile to connect our camera to prepare for camera calibration.

9
00:01:08.140 --> 00:01:16.140
So to start with that, we want to move up here to this area in our toolbar so that we can move to our media profile section.

10
00:01:16.140 --> 00:01:23.519
So first, I'm going to click this button, and this button is going to allow me to create a new empty media profile.

11
00:01:23.519 --> 00:01:28.519
Now, when this pops up to pick a media profile class, we're going to choose media profile.

12
00:01:28.519 --> 00:01:34.709
Once that's selected, it's going to provide us another window that is going to ask where we're going to put this.

13
00:01:34.709 --> 00:01:45.709
Now, since we're going to be using our media profile to actually feed the camera's view into the engine for camera calibration, we want to create a new folder and call that calibration.

14
00:01:45.709 --> 00:01:52.000
Then we can go ahead and double-click to select that folder, and then we need to name our media profile.

15
00:01:52.000 --> 00:02:01.000
For our media profile, we want to name it something that we're actually going to be able to recognize and switch to whenever we use this calibration for a specific camera.

16
00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:03.000
So we're going to start with MP for media profile.

17
00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:10.000
We're going to name it Latte because we are on the Latte stage, BM for Blackmagic, and Aja for our Aja Key Pro.

18
00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:12.000
I'm going to go ahead and hit save.

19
00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:16.000
Once that happens, you're going to see a menu pop up that looks something like this.

20
00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:29.030
Now, in order to make sure that you've actually got a good profile and you're not hanging on to anything that exists from a previous media profile, you're going to see this nice red bar that says this project doesn't have the media proxies configured.

21
00:02:29.030 --> 00:02:35.030
To get started, we are going to click configure now inside our red warning menu.

22
00:02:35.030 --> 00:02:41.030
Once that happens, a new window is going to pop up and give us the option for our media profile configuration.

23
00:02:41.030 --> 00:02:46.030
From there, we're going to choose our proxies location and we're going to choose our calibration folder.

24
00:02:46.030 --> 00:02:48.030
That'll generate our proxy folder.

25
00:02:48.030 --> 00:02:50.030
Same thing for our bundles location.

26
00:02:50.030 --> 00:02:52.030
We're going to choose our calibration folder.

27
00:02:52.030 --> 00:02:58.030
Now, under our number of source proxies, we're going to go ahead and change this from two to one.

28
00:02:58.030 --> 00:03:03.030
And then for our output proxies, we have the option here of leaving this as one or selecting zero.

29
00:03:03.030 --> 00:03:07.030
Since we want to actually set our output proxy, we're going to leave this as one.

30
00:03:07.030 --> 00:03:13.030
Now, you want to make sure that the should create bundle is checked on and then go ahead and hit configure.

31
00:03:13.030 --> 00:03:18.030
This will change our media profile window and configure the actual media profile for us to use.

32
00:03:18.030 --> 00:03:24.030
Now, once that's done, let's move back into our calibration folder and choose our media profile.

33
00:03:24.030 --> 00:03:27.030
This is our MP Latte Blackmagic Aja profile.

34
00:03:27.030 --> 00:03:33.030
You can see this question mark that is here and the other media profile sources automatically added themselves to this configuration.

35
00:03:34.030 --> 00:03:39.099
Now, in order to get this ready to go, before I do this, I want to be able to save this.

36
00:03:39.099 --> 00:03:42.099
So, I want to go to source control and make sure I mark this for add.

37
00:03:42.099 --> 00:03:49.099
That way I can make changes and save this as needed and it will actually make changes and save them to the project on Perforce.

38
00:03:49.099 --> 00:03:52.099
Now, let's double click and reopen our media profile.

39
00:03:52.099 --> 00:03:57.379
Now, you'll see that the nice red bar that warned us that we didn't have a configuration is gone.

40
00:03:57.379 --> 00:04:02.379
Now, we need to actually go through and start creating our media profile source selections.

41
00:04:02.379 --> 00:04:05.379
So, the first thing we want to do is go under our input section here.

42
00:04:05.379 --> 00:04:10.770
I'm going to make this a little bit smaller so you can see it's not quite as wide so I don't have to move left and right.

43
00:04:10.770 --> 00:04:13.770
And that way it's a little bit more compact and easier to see.

44
00:04:13.770 --> 00:04:16.769
Now, I'm going to start here under inputs and I'm going to move to media source.

45
00:04:16.769 --> 00:04:20.769
And you can see that there is one array element because we have one source.

46
00:04:20.769 --> 00:04:25.769
Now, I'm going to click on the media source 01 and choose my Aja media source.

47
00:04:25.769 --> 00:04:31.769
Next, I'm going to expand that because I have new options available after selecting my source.

48
00:04:31.769 --> 00:04:36.769
From my Aja's media source option, I want to go ahead and expand some of these.

49
00:04:36.769 --> 00:04:42.769
So, first, I'm going to select my Aja and I'm going to go ahead and select my configuration.

50
00:04:42.769 --> 00:04:48.769
And under my configuration, I want to make sure that I am at single length 1, that my resolution is HD 1080p,

51
00:04:48.769 --> 00:04:54.769
and that my standard is set to progressive and that my frame rate is actually set to 24 frames per second

52
00:04:54.769 --> 00:04:57.769
since we're shooting with a 24 frames per second camera.

53
00:04:57.769 --> 00:05:01.769
Then go ahead and hit apply and this will actually configure that option.

54
00:05:01.769 --> 00:05:04.769
Next, I want to choose my timecode format.

55
00:05:04.769 --> 00:05:10.769
Now, I want to choose the LTC format, but you want to be able to choose whatever format you're actually using.

56
00:05:10.769 --> 00:05:15.769
Once that's done, I want to move a little bit further down into my video section

57
00:05:15.769 --> 00:05:18.769
and where I've got my color format, I want to make some changes.

58
00:05:18.769 --> 00:05:23.769
So, first, I want to change from 8-bit YUV and change that to a 10-bit format.

59
00:05:23.769 --> 00:05:27.769
Then I want to change my is sRGB input to on.

60
00:05:27.769 --> 00:05:34.769
Once that's done, then my sRGB format is selected and my media source is finished.

61
00:05:34.769 --> 00:05:37.769
Now, if I have more than one media source or more than one camera,

62
00:05:37.769 --> 00:05:41.769
I can go ahead and repeat these steps for a second media source.

63
00:05:41.769 --> 00:05:43.769
Next, I want to move into my outputs.

64
00:05:43.769 --> 00:05:47.769
In my outputs, it's going to work pretty similar to what we did for our inputs.

65
00:05:47.769 --> 00:05:52.769
I'm going to go in and first select my media source and choose my Aja media output.

66
00:05:52.769 --> 00:05:56.769
Next, I'm going to expand those options and choose my Aja again.

67
00:05:56.769 --> 00:06:00.769
Now, my Aja configuration, I can go ahead and hit this

68
00:06:00.769 --> 00:06:03.769
and you're going to see the same options here with a few more options available.

69
00:06:03.769 --> 00:06:06.769
I have output type as fill and fill and key,

70
00:06:06.769 --> 00:06:09.769
and with that, I'm going to go ahead and make sure that this is set as fill.

71
00:06:09.769 --> 00:06:12.769
Since we're not actually doing any color keying, we're going to use Kona.

72
00:06:12.769 --> 00:06:15.769
I want to change this from single link one to single link two.

73
00:06:15.769 --> 00:06:17.769
Next, we're going to make sure that this is HD 1080,

74
00:06:17.769 --> 00:06:20.769
and then we're going to make sure that this is also progressive

75
00:06:20.769 --> 00:06:23.769
and change our frame rate to 24 frames per second.

76
00:06:23.769 --> 00:06:25.769
We're going to leave our reference as free run.

77
00:06:25.769 --> 00:06:27.769
Then I'm going to go ahead and hit apply,

78
00:06:27.769 --> 00:06:29.769
and I'm going to move down to my output options.

79
00:06:29.769 --> 00:06:33.769
Now, my output options, I'm going to go ahead and make the same changes

80
00:06:33.769 --> 00:06:35.769
to my timecode format.

81
00:06:35.769 --> 00:06:37.769
I'm going to first verify that this is LTC

82
00:06:37.769 --> 00:06:41.769
and then change my pixel format from 8-bit YUV to 10-bit YUV.

83
00:06:41.769 --> 00:06:44.769
Now, that finishes my output setup,

84
00:06:44.769 --> 00:06:46.769
and now we need to move on to the next section,

85
00:06:46.769 --> 00:06:49.769
which is our timecode provider and our genlock provider.

86
00:06:49.769 --> 00:06:52.769
Now, for our timecode setup, we want to scroll down

87
00:06:52.769 --> 00:06:57.769
and choose to check on override project settings.

88
00:06:57.769 --> 00:06:59.769
Then we want to choose our timecode provider

89
00:06:59.769 --> 00:07:01.769
and choose our Aja SDI input.

90
00:07:01.769 --> 00:07:03.769
Then from there, let's expand our provider,

91
00:07:03.769 --> 00:07:05.769
go down to timecode, and then we'll see

92
00:07:05.769 --> 00:07:07.769
we have some other options that we can choose.

93
00:07:07.769 --> 00:07:09.769
We want to use a dedicated pin.

94
00:07:09.769 --> 00:07:11.769
We don't want to use reference in

95
00:07:11.769 --> 00:07:13.769
because that will conflict with our genlock.

96
00:07:13.769 --> 00:07:16.769
And then we want to change our LTC configuration

97
00:07:16.769 --> 00:07:19.769
and make sure that we are using 24 frames per second.

98
00:07:19.769 --> 00:07:22.990
Notice, we don't have to choose an SDI input.

99
00:07:22.990 --> 00:07:26.990
So with these options, we are set with our Kona 5,

100
00:07:26.990 --> 00:07:29.990
our LTC index is 1, and our 24 frame rate selected.

101
00:07:29.990 --> 00:07:32.990
Hit apply, and now let's move into our genlock.

102
00:07:32.990 --> 00:07:34.990
In our genlock, I'm going to go ahead

103
00:07:34.990 --> 00:07:36.990
and override my project settings again,

104
00:07:36.990 --> 00:07:38.990
which will activate my custom timestamp,

105
00:07:38.990 --> 00:07:41.990
and from there, I'm going to choose my Aja SDI input.

106
00:07:41.990 --> 00:07:44.990
Now, I can expand my custom timestamp and my genlock,

107
00:07:44.990 --> 00:07:47.990
and I want to make sure that I click on use reference in.

108
00:07:47.990 --> 00:07:50.990
And from there, I can choose my configuration.

109
00:07:50.990 --> 00:07:52.990
So from here, I'm going to choose my Kona 5.

110
00:07:52.990 --> 00:07:55.990
I'm going to change my single link to single link 4.

111
00:07:55.990 --> 00:07:57.990
And then from here, I've got my 1080p resolution,

112
00:07:57.990 --> 00:07:59.990
progressive standard, and again,

113
00:07:59.990 --> 00:08:01.990
change my frame rate to 24 frames per second.

114
00:08:01.990 --> 00:08:04.990
With that finished, I can go ahead and hit apply.

115
00:08:04.990 --> 00:08:06.990
And now with all my options finished,

116
00:08:06.990 --> 00:08:08.990
I can move up here to the upper left-hand corner

117
00:08:08.990 --> 00:08:12.990
of my media profile and go ahead and hit apply

118
00:08:12.990 --> 00:08:16.990
and then save my media profile to finish this setup.

119
00:08:16.990 --> 00:08:19.990
Now that we've finished our media profile configuration,

120
00:08:19.990 --> 00:08:21.990
we can go ahead and hand this back over to Brian

121
00:08:21.990 --> 00:08:25.990
to continue with an ICDFX cinematography discussion

122
00:08:25.990 --> 00:08:27.990
about considerations and techniques.
